{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>My strength and the song of YH.</b> Rabbi Moses said: the resh of זמרת has a kamatz, and it is known by its accent as though it were עזי וזמרתי, and like it: אם אתן שנת לעיני, which is like שנתי; אף נחלת שפרה — עלי נחלתי. The answer: we find the kamatz in construct state, as in ה׳ מנת חלקי וכוסי — and one could read it thus: HaShem is my portion and my cup. If so, what will be done with the word ומנת המלך?! Others said: the yod of עזי is added, the proof being that it has a kamatz chatuf and not a shureq, like ה׳ עזי ומעוזי. But what will be done, since it is written: כי חקך הטריפני לחם חקי, ה׳ בעזך ישמח מלך, נהלת בעזך — there is no difference between them. And furthermore: what is the reason for the vav of ויהי לי לישועה?! And I say: אם אתן שנת לעיני — סמוך to עיני, and the lamed comes added like לימין לבית, and there is no doubt that לימין is construct. And likewise מנת, and אף נחלת — construct, and the construct word is deficient, like ושכורה ולא מיין; and we are not concerned that it is נחלת with a kamatz. And thus the grammatical explanation of עזי וזמרת יה: construct. And the word עזי governs another word, like יכפה אף. And so it is: עזי וזמרת עזי יה — עזי is my strength, כחי, and the beginning of my strength, like הוא השם; or עזי וזמרת יה — עזי."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 118, :notes {0 "I read the phrase 'וכן הוא עזי וזמרת עזי יה עזי כחי ותחלת כחי' as a compressed chain illustrating how עזי distributes across multiple constructs; the parsing is cryptic and the clause division uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:06.088907690Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}